    "# AAI-520 — Integrated Investment Research Agent\n",
    "\n",
    "**Group 5:** Hyunju Yu (Student 1: data/NLP), Jim McCarthy (Student 2:\n",
    "planning, tools, routing and memory), Glen Salazar (Student 3: specialists,\n",
    "evaluation and reporting).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Team repository:** [bigthinkertoo/aai-520-g5](https://github.com/bigthinkertoo/aai-520-g5)\n",
    "\n",
    "One shared DataBundle connects acquisition → preprocessing → classify → extract → summarize → digest → specialists → evaluate → revise → report → reflection and memory. Student ownership remains visible below.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Setup and operating modes\n",
    "\n",
    "Use Python 3.10+ in the selected notebook kernel. Install `numpy pandas matplotlib ipython`; live mode also needs `requests yfinance feedparser` and the selected `openai` or `anthropic` SDK. Optional: `python-dotenv`, `nltk` and an already installed VADER lexicon. This notebook performs no package installation or downloads.\n",
    "\n",
    "`LIVE=1` in the environment enables external requests and potentially paid LLM calls. The default is a labeled synthetic demo with the actual Student 1 assembler and NLP chain. Keep API keys in environment variables or local `.env` (not Git). SEC access requires `SEC_USER_AGENT` with a real contact; NewsAPI and Alpha Vantage keys are optional. Select manual source controls with `USE_MANUAL_SOURCES=1`; otherwise the planner selects groups."
   ]
