    "## Step 19 — Routing and Student 3 contracts\n",
    "\n",
    "`route_content(bundle)` creates earnings, news and market packets only for requested source groups. Each packet preserves the symbol, timestamp, requested groups, sample flag and citation URLs; news records retain article IDs. References identify evidence but do not alone prove claim support.\n",
    "\n",
    "The integrated agent uses these callable interfaces:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `analyst(role, packet, feedback=None, lessons=None) -> dict`: implemented by `analyze_packet`. The first draft receives saved lessons; a revised draft also receives evaluator feedback. Custom analysts must accept both keywords and return JSON-serializable role analysis with evidence-backed claims, risks and limitations.\n",
    "- `evaluator(bundle, analyses, plan) -> dict`: implemented by `evaluate_research`. Required validated fields are `score` (finite 0–1), `issues` (list of strings), and `retry_news` (boolean). The revision loop additionally consumes `needs_revision` (boolean) and `analysis_feedback` (mapping from routed role to feedback). Use the same scoring policy for every draft and retrieval pass.\n",
    "- `reporter(bundle, analyses, evaluation) -> dict`: implemented by `build_report`. The displayed report requires `markdown`; the integrated report also includes `recommendation`. Setting `reporter=None` returns an evidence handoff instead, which does not have the displayed Markdown-report interface.\n",
    "\n",
    "Student 2 owns planning, tool management, routing, bounded orchestration and persistence. Student 3 supplies specialist analysis, evaluation, report building and analytical reflection. The shared `call_llm` records model calls. Diagnostic scores and numeric gates do not certify factual accuracy, semantic support, fiscal-period matching or completeness. Synthetic runs remain labeled and receive no investment rating.\n"
   ]
  },
