    "## Step 22 — Research evaluation\n",
    "\n",
    "The evaluator reports:\n",
    "* source coverage, \n",
    "* data-quality checks, \n",
    "* numeric-gate failure rate, \n",
    "* evidence-reference/value checks, and\n",
    "* composite diagnostic score.\n",
    "\n",
    "Where Alpha Vantage is available, it also reports aggregate sentiment-sign agreement. None of these is a measured overall hallucination rate or investment confidence."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2bd5aa8f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Coverage measures requested source groups with available data. Numeric-gate failure rate is failed extraction/summary checks divided by checks performed; it is `None` when no such checks ran. Sentiment agreement compares signs of aggregate scores, not labeled sentiment accuracy. The composite weights are classroom design choices, not calibrated probabilities.\n",
    "\n",
    "Gate details retain the article ID, title, detected issue and handling action. A rejected figure is removed before summarization, but all remaining recorded gate failures still block a rating pending review. The composite score cannot override that block."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 32,
   "id": "team-revised-052",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Owner: Student 3 — Glen Salazar: analysis and quality\n",
    "def evaluate_research(bundle: dict, analyses: dict, plan: dict) -> dict:\n",
    "    market, fund, news = (\n",
    "        bundle[\"market\"],\n",
    "        bundle[\"fundamentals\"],\n",
    "        bundle[\"news\"],\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    articles = news.get(\"articles\", [])\n",
    "    info = fund.get(\"company_info\") or {}\n",
    "    available = {\n",
    "        \"prices\": bool(market.get(\"price_summary\")),\n",
    "        \"peers\": bool(market.get(\"peers\")),\n",
    "        \"fundamentals\": bool(info) and bool(fund.get(\"key_financials\")),\n",
    "        \"sec\": bool(bundle.get(\"filings\")),\n",
    "        \"macro\": bool(bundle.get(\"macro\")),\n",
    "        \"news\": len(articles) >= 3,\n",
    "        \"alphavantage\": bool(bundle[\"external_sentiment\"].get(\"alphavantage\")),\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    selected = plan[\"sources\"]\n",
    "    coverage = sum(available[s] for s in selected) / len(selected)\n",
    "    issues = [f\"missing_or_thin:{s}\" for s in selected if not available[s]]\n",
    "    checks = [available[s] for s in selected]\n",
    "    if \"fundamentals\" in selected:\n",
    "        checks.append(\n",
    "            sum(\n",
    "                info.get(k) is not None\n",
    "                for k in [\n",
    "                    \"trailingPE\",\n",
    "                    \"forwardPE\",\n",
    "                    \"profitMargins\",\n",
    "                    \"revenueGrowth\",\n",
    "                    \"marketCap\",\n",
    "                ]\n",
    "            )\n",
    "            >= 3\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    if \"prices\" in selected:\n",
    "        date = (market.get(\"price_summary\") or {}).get(\"last_date\")\n",
    "        age = (\n",
    "            (\n",
    "                datetime.now(timezone.utc).date() - pd.Timestamp(date).date()\n",
    "            ).days\n",
    "            if date\n",
    "            else 999\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        checks.append(0 <= age <= CONFIG[\"THRESHOLDS\"][\"max_price_age_days\"])\n",
    "        if not checks[-1]:\n",
    "            issues.append(\"price_missing_or_stale\")\n",
    "    if \"news\" in selected:\n",
    "        publishers = {a[\"article\"].get(\"publisher\") for a in articles}\n",
    "        checks.append(len(publishers - {None, \"\"}) >= 2)\n",
    "        if articles and all(a.get(\"method\") != \"llm\" for a in articles):\n",
    "            issues.append(\"nlp_uses_rules\")\n",
    "    gates = bundle[\"pipeline_meta\"].get(\"gates\", {})\n",
    "    numeric_gates = [gates.get(k, {}) for k in [\"2_extract\", \"3_summarize\"]]\n",
    "    checked = sum(g.get(\"checked\", 0) for g in numeric_gates)\n",
    "    failed = sum(g.get(\"failed\", 0) for g in numeric_gates)\n",
    "    gate_failure_rate = failed / checked if checked else None\n",
    "    for failure in bundle[\"pipeline_meta\"].get(\"gate_failures\", []):\n",
    "        issues.append(\"gate_failure:\" + failure[\"gate\"])\n",
    "    if news.get(\"digest\", {}).get(\"ungrounded_numbers\"):\n",
    "        issues.append(\"digest_has_ungrounded_numbers\")\n",
    "    av = bundle[\"external_sentiment\"].get(\"alphavantage\") or []\n",
    "    scores = [\n",
    "        a[\"ticker_sentiment\"] for a in av if a.get(\"ticker_relevance\", 0) > 0.2\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "    agreement = None\n",
    "    if scores and articles:\n",
    "        agreement = float(\n",
    "            np.sign(np.mean(scores))\n",
    "            == np.sign(news[\"aggregate\"][\"weighted_score\"])\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        if not agreement:\n",
    "            issues.append(\"sentiment_divergence\")\n",
    "    synthetic = bundle[\"pipeline_meta\"].get(\"mode\") == \"demo\" or news.get(\n",
    "        \"used_sample_data\", False\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    if synthetic:\n",
    "        issues.append(\"synthetic_data_not_real_evidence\")\n",
    "    quality = sum(checks) / len(checks)\n",
    "    score = (coverage + quality) / 2\n",
    "    if gate_failure_rate is not None:\n",
    "        score *= 1 - gate_failure_rate\n",
    "    if \"digest_has_ungrounded_numbers\" in issues:\n",
    "        score *= 0.75\n",
    "    if synthetic:\n",
    "        score *= 0.75\n",
    "    audit = analysis_audit(bundle, analyses)\n",
    "    issues.extend(audit[\"issues\"])\n",
    "    score = 0.7 * score + 0.3 * audit[\"score\"]\n",
    "    article_titles = {a[\"article\"][\"id\"]: a[\"article\"][\"title\"] for a in articles}\n",
    "    gate_details = [\n",
    "        {\"gate\": failure[\"gate\"], \"article_id\": failure.get(\"article_id\"),\n",
    "         \"title\": article_titles.get(failure.get(\"article_id\"), \"Aggregate or unavailable\"),\n",
    "         \"issues\": failure.get(\"issues\", []),\n",
    "         \"handling\": \"Rejected figures removed before summarization; review remaining fields\"\n",
    "             if failure[\"gate\"] == \"2_extract\" else \"Review gate output and fallback; rating withheld\"}\n",
    "        for failure in bundle[\"pipeline_meta\"].get(\"gate_failures\", [])\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"gate_details\": gate_details,\n",
    "        \"score\": round(score, 3),\n",
    "        \"analysis_score\": audit[\"score\"],\n",
    "        \"analysis_feedback\": audit[\"feedback\"],\n",
    "        \"needs_revision\": bool(audit[\"issues\"]),\n",
    "        \"issues\": list(dict.fromkeys(issues)),\n",
    "        \"retry_news\": \"news\" in selected and len(articles) < 3,\n",
    "        \"metric\": \"data_and_analysis_diagnostics_not_accuracy\",\n",
    "        \"breakdown\": {\n",
    "            \"coverage\": coverage,\n",
    "            \"data_quality\": quality,\n",
    "            \"numeric_gate_pass_rate\": (\n",
    "                None if not checked else 1 - gate_failure_rate\n",
    "            ),\n",
    "            \"sentiment_agreement\": agreement,\n",
    "        },\n",
    "        \"numeric_gate_failure_rate\": gate_failure_rate,\n",
    "        \"ready_for_final_report\": not synthetic and not issues,\n",
    "    }\n"
   ]
  },
