    "## Rubric mapping and results\n",
    "\n",
    "| Requirement | Implementation and visible evidence |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Plans research | Validated registry-aware source plan; manual selection also retained |\n",
    "| Dynamic tools | Selected groups expand to registered tools; source skipping and failures audited |\n",
    "| Self-reflection | Analysis feedback, revision history and saved reflection shown below the report |\n",
    "| Learns across runs | Controlled synthetic first/second-run comparison shows a predefined lesson changing draft behavior; Step 28 separates this from live learning |\n",
    "| Prompt chaining | Student 1 classify → extract → summarize → digest, with intermediate demonstration cells |\n",
    "| Routing | Role packets plus earnings/news/market specialist outputs |\n",
    "| Evaluator–optimizer | Deliberately flawed draft → feedback → corrected draft; wider retrieval is a separate action |\n",
    "| Code/documentation | Shared contracts, labeled modes, checks, diagram, chart, GitHub link and README |\n",
    "\n",
    "## Limitations and conclusion\n",
    "\n",
    "The live run demonstrates LLM-based source planning,\n",
    "data collection, specialist routing, evaluation, reporting and persistent\n",
    "memory. Earnings and market specialists used the LLM; the news specialist\n",
    "used its rule-based fallback because the evidence exceeded the 30,000-character\n",
    "limit. Yahoo Finance news failed after three attempts, but the workflow\n",
    "continued with the other selected providers. The overall diagnostic score\n",
    "was 0.986. A summary-gate failure remained, so the report correctly returned\n",
    "`INSUFFICIENT EVIDENCE / NO RATING`. The flagged number requires source review;\n",
    "the diagnostic score does not establish factual accuracy or investment confidence.\n",
    "\n",
    "The controlled offline checks passed, including revision, memory adaptation,\n",
    "source routing, contract validation and failure handling. In the separate\n",
    "live fixed-evidence comparison, supplying saved lessons increased the analysis\n",
    "diagnostic score from approximately 0.917 to 1.000 and reduced flagged issues\n",
    "from one to zero. This is evidence of improvement in this observed pair, not\n",
    "proof of general learning: both conditions included LLM and rule-based outputs,\n",
    "the lesson categories are predefined, and model randomness may affect results.\n",
    "Repeated comparisons and independent claim review are still needed.\n",
    "\n",
    "Step 28's excerpt judgments are AI-assisted, and student source reviews remain\n",
    "pending. Evidence references and copied-value checks cannot verify every\n",
    "interpretation or identify all missing facts. News is snippet based, and SEC\n",
    "comparisons require matching periods and units. Numeric checks, including\n",
    "simple number-word normalization, can still produce false positives or miss\n",
    "semantic errors. JSON memory is single-writer and bounded to ten runs per\n",
    "symbol; demo and live memory must remain separate. Provider behavior and model\n",
    "availability can change. Overall, the live run demonstrates the integrated\n",
    "workflow and its safeguards, while the remaining caveats limit the report's\n",
    "use to a classroom research demonstration.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Recommendation for future research\n",
    "\n",
    "Future research using investment AI agents should look at using FinBERT,\n",
    "an NLP model based on BERT that tackles financial domain problems. According\n",
    "to Araci (2019), FinBERT is effective in nuanced sentiment analysis,\n",
    "and suggests it can help with making financial interpretations and decision making. Another\n",
    "avenue for future research is to use FinRobot (Yang et al., 2024), an open-source\n",
    "AI agent platform that uses financially specialized LLMs in multiple layers\n",
    "for advanced financial analysis and decision making. Thus, future research can\n",
    "incorporate FinBERT and/or FinRobot in making financial evaluations using NLP and LLM based agents.\n",
